      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is a problem I've encountered as well, here is my example:\nI've made a toggleable spear parented to the left hand. \nI want it to be grabbable by my right hand and by other players, however there is no way to limit which local hand is able to grab it, only an universal disable grabbing toggle.\nToggling it ON breaks the left hand grab as it will always grab to the spear and never to other physbones, it will enable other players and my right hand to grab it though.\nToggling it OFF will just disable grabbing which is not what I want. Using a constraint would work, but would prevent other players from grabbing it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-22T23:31:43.492Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There are several occurrences where I have created a gimmick that involves putting a PhysBone at the location of the hand.\nThese PhysBone gimmicks are either intended to be grabbed by either the opposite hand, or any hand of another player (left or right).\nFor example, if I am making an item located on my left hand that has a handle which can be pulled, I want that item to be only grabbable only by my own right hand, or by another player's hand (their left hand or their right hand).\nHowever, due to the PhysBone being located on the left hand, closing the left hand grip will grab the bone, as a non intentional action.\nMy request would be for avatar creators to have a way to prevent these accidental grabs from happening.",
